# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Enable BLS BEEFY (ecdsa_bls381 paired keys) on Westend testnet

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Switches the BEEFY key type on the Westend runtime from plain ecdsa to paired
      ecdsa_bls381 keys. This result in making many applications of BLS signatures
      possible on Westend testnet  including signature aggregation for an efficient
      BEEFY bridge to Ethereum.

      - Enable `bls-experimental` feature on `pallet-beefy-mmr` in the Westend runtime.
      - Use `BeefyEcdsaBls381ToEthereum` as the merkle leaf converter.
      - Update the westend emulated chain genesis to use `ecdsa_bls_crypto::AuthorityId`.
      - Add `PairedCrypto::left_public` / `right_public` helper methods on `sp-core`.

      Note: The MMR leaf currently commits to ECDSA keys only (extracted from the
      paired keys) for backward compatibility with legacy bridges. To enable BLS aggregate
      signature verification on Ethereum, a polynomial commitment to the BLS public
      keys is needed for APK proofs. This commitment could either be added to the
      `BeefyAuthoritySet::keyset_commitment` (by tupling multiple commitments) or
      stored in a parachain block and proven via the parachain heads root already
      present in the MMR leaf.
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      The polkadot node binary now supports a `bls-beefy-experimental` feature flag that
      switches the BEEFY authority ID type from `ecdsa_crypto` to `ecdsa_bls_crypto`
      (paired ecdsa + bls381 keys). This propagates through `polkadot-cli` and
      `polkadot-service`.
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      Westend validators will now use paired ecdsa_bls381 keys for BEEFY instead of
      plain ecdsa keys. The node binary must be built with `--features bls-beefy-experimental`
      to enable this. Validators will need to rotate their BEEFY session keys after this
      change is deployed.

crates:
  - name: westend-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: westend-emulated-chain
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot-service
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot-cli
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot
    bump: patch
  - name: pallet-beefy-mmr
    bump: patch
  - name: sp-core
    bump: minor
  - name: sc-consensus-beefy
    bump: patch
